-----------------------
(1) SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS
-----------------------

  Linux kernel version 2.2.X or 2.4.X
  Pentium class processor 300 MHz (500 MHz recommended)
  64 MB RAM required (128 MB recommended)
  glibc 2.1
  Supported 3D accelerator card
  XFree86 version 4.0.2 or newer
  OSS compatible sound card
  Hard disk drive with 600 MB of available space


------------------
(2) INSTALLATION
------------------

The Linux client installation also installs a dedicated server, so if you
already have the dedicated server installed, you must first remove it with
"loki_uninstall" before you install the game.

Log in, mount the Tribes 2 CD and change the current directory to where
it is mounted.  Type 'sh setup.sh' to run the install script.

e.g.  Log in as root:
	mount /mnt/cdrom
	cd /mnt/cdrom
	sh setup.sh

If you haven't already installed the Loki Update Tool or Loki Uninstall
Tool, the installer will prompt you to install these before installing
the main product.

Once the installation is complete, the update tool will be run to ensure
that you have the latest updates to the game.  No information about you
is sent to the server during this process, and this does not register
your product.


--------------------
(3) PLAYING THE GAME
--------------------

    The manual is available in PDF format in the file "Tribes2_Manual.pdf"
    in the installation directory.  The best viewer for this is the Adobe
    Acrobat reader, available at: http://www.adobe.com/products/acrobat/

    Run 'tribes2' to start the game.

    The first time you run the game it will create a .loki/tribes2
    directory in your home directory.  Saved games, temporary files,
    and preferences will be stored here.

    The following arguments may be given to Tribes 2:

        [-h | --help]           Display this help message
        [-v | --version]        Display the game version
        [-f | --fullscreen]     Run the game fullscreen
        [-w | --windowed]       Run the game in a window
        [-s | --nosound]        Do not access the soundcard
        [-u | --update]         Run the Loki auto-update tool
        [-q | --qagent]         Run the Loki QAgent support tool
        [-g | --gllibrary]      Select 3D rendering library

    String widgets have standard UNIX keybindings.

        Ctrl-A - Move to beginning of line
        Ctrl-E - Move to end of line
        Ctrl-B - Move backwards
        Ctrl-F - Move forwards
        Ctrl-U - Erase line
        Ctrl-D - Delete character
        Ctrl-C - Copy to X clipboard
        Ctrl-V - Paste from X clipboard

    For information on the dedicated server, check out README.tribes2d


-------------------    
(4) TROUBLESHOOTING    
-------------------    
The following are some of the more common problems you might have, and
recommended solutions:

A) The game runs very slowly

   As of this writing, the only video cards for which we offer
   configuration support are the nVidia cards with the 0.9-769
   drivers.  You can get the latest nVidia drivers from
   http://www.nvidia.com/

   However, the game has been tested as playable with the following cards
   (using the DRI drivers):
      ATI: Rage 128, Rage 128 Pro, Radeon
   This requires the use of the DRI drivers compiled from CVS.
   This is not supported, but if you want to try this, you should
   follow their instructions for compilation and installation:
   http://dri.sourceforge.net/

   You may want to adjust graphics settings in order to choose the
   visual quality vs. performance level you are comfortable with.

B) I have a sound card, but I'm not getting any sound.
   
   First, make certain that you have your sound drivers configured
   correctly, and that your speakers are on and correctly connected.
   
   Second, if you are using a desktop environment (e.g. GNOME or
   KDE) which uses sound, make certain that the sound daemon associated
   with the environment (esd or artsd) is not grabbing /dev/dsp and
   preventing sounds from being played.

C) I used --nosound and I can't get sound back

   To reenable sound, you must delete the line about OpenAL in:
   ~/.loki/tribes2/base/prefs/ClientPrefs.cs


